  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \nAn area of showers and thunderstorms back across Illinois and \nIndiana will continue to move slowly east this afternoon into early \nevening in association with a weak embedded mid level short wave. The\nairmass over our area remains in a bit of an instability min though,\nso there is some uncertainty as to how well this activity will hold \ntogether as it approaches our area. Meanwhile, a weak low level jet \nwill shift east toward our area later tonight and some of the hi-res \nCAMs are trying to show scattered redevelopment associated with \nthis. Will therefore show two periods of higher pops (but still limit\nthem to chance or less) later this afternoon into early evening and \nthen again later tonight into early Friday morning. Better chances \nfor showers and thunderstorms will then develop Friday afternoon into\nFriday night as a somewhat stronger mid level short wave moves east \nacross the mid Ohio Valley.\n\nA broad, shallow upper level trough will then be in place across the\nGreat Lakes region through the weekend and into early next week. \nGenerally weak, embedded mid level short waves moving through the \ntrough will lead to occasional chances for showers and thunderstorms\nat times. While it will be tough to rule out a few stronger storms, \nthe overall severe threat will remain fairly limited in the nearer \nterm due to the lack of deeper shear. \n\nLonger range guidance is suggesting the upper level trough will \nbegin to deepen over the Great Lakes and Ohio Valley region later in\nthe period. This will lead to better chances for showers and \nthunderstorms as we head into mid next week, along with somewhat \ncooler temperatures.",
